{{define "communication"}}
Ordinary progress, milestones and resolved intermediate failures go in the ledger. Send only when someone must act, decide, or avoid a mistaken wait; question request is for actual blockers. Submissions, evidence and gates already notify the right people; add only an action, changed conclusion or missing context. Contact master when acceptance must change or a gate must be released. Developers and reviewers discuss findings directly and consolidate related points. Answer requests with message reply; never reply to pure acknowledgments or obsolete task notices. These are judgment guidelines, not message quotas: surface real blockers and time-sensitive risks promptly.
{{end}}
